<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32537" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ŏlynthus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , 1, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄλυνθος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Thrace</i>, <i>on
				the borders of Macedonia</i>, now <i>Agia
			Maria</i>, or <i>Aio Mamas</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 2,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11, 18, § 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep. Pel. 1,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 12, 47</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Olynthius</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Olynthus</i>, <i>Olynthian</i>, <i><span class="en">Curt. 8, 8,
				19</span></i>. —Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Olynthĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>the region about
				Olynthus</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1,
			44</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Olynthius</span></b> , ii,
				m., <i>an Olynthian</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 5, 10,
			34</span></i>.—Usually in plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Olyn-thii</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Olynthus</i>, <i>the
			Olynthians</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Timoth. 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 8, 3,
				10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 4,
			6</span></i>. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
